   (LvSIRT6). Remarkably, niacinamide supplementation after hemocyanin
   knockdown restored hemolymph microbial balance, reduced Vibrio
   dominance, and improved shrimp survival against V. parahaemolyticus
   infection, but not Gram-positive Staphylococcus aureus (Sa). These
   findings provide novel insights into the pivotal role of niacinamide
   metabolism in regulating shrimp hemolymph microbial composition via
